@startuml runtime_usage_provenance
' Source baseline: Java 001a37d0; pi 4af9d21d3b4d664e4a29fcabfec85171077248e3.
' Java: modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/types/Usage.java#fromJson/empty.
' Java: modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/provider/openai/OpenAICompletionsProvider.java#handleChunk.
' Java: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java#usageRecord.
' pi: packages/ai/src/types.ts:382; packages/ai/src/api/openai-responses.ts:118.
' Observed behavior: numeric zero alone does not prove a provider usage report.
' Design reason: preserve reported zero without inventing usage for missing reports.
' Java divergence: internal provenance supports the CampusClaw public omission contract.
title Usage provenance and JSON restoration
start
if (Provider reports usage?) then (yes)
  :Usage with known = true;
else (no)
  :Usage.empty with known = false;
endif
:Persist internal Usage JSON;
if (JSON contains known?) then (yes)
  :Restore the explicit provenance;
else (legacy)
  if (Any token value is nonzero?) then (yes)
    :Restore known = true;
  else (no)
    :Restore known = false;
  endif
endif
:Return internal Usage to its caller;
stop
@enduml
